 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling, punctuation and syllables, as sung. \"dov' è\" and \"Cos' è\" are printed on two notes and kept as two words. Lines are repeated as the score repeats them; Leporello's broken-off phrases keep the print's dashes. In the closing \"certo è l'ombra\" the print has Elvira, Zerlina, Ottavio and Masetto sing \"che m'incontrò\" and only Donna Anna \"che l'incontrò\" (the libretto gives m'incontrò to Elvira alone); the words follow the print. In bar 100 the print sets Anna's words as \"cer-tò e\" (the accent on the wrong vowel), and Ottavio's and Masetto's as \"e\" without its accent; these clear misprints are corrected to \"certo è\", as Zerlina's line prints it. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S61), and the IPA was checked against Castel. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
